Exact decimal binary128 literals in the pinned bare-metal RV64 image.

Newlib 4.5.0.20241231 strtold writes x87 into binary128 storage. Its
_strtodg_l also fails boundary tests at 113-bit nearest and 114-bit directed
rounding. Reuse its integer bignum helpers (mprec) without the approximate
floating conversion path: construct the exact rational, divide at the
binary128 quantum and round once, ties to even. See results/model/ld-literals.md.

Only compiler literal parsing changes; public libc strtold is unchanged.
Applies after 0001/0002 and slot 1's 0003 (disjoint preprocessor/C11 work).
The pristine vendor/tinycc and existing sum compile-cut stay untouched.

--- a/tccpp.c
